Private KP patch: RTL8831BU and confirmed RTL8851B USB IDs

The Realtek-authored upstream Linux rtw8851bu table binds b831/b851,
D-Link 332a, Mercusys 0128, TP-Link 010b and Edimax e611 to the same
rtw8851b chip implementation (ff/ff/ff interface only).
The vendor driver biglinux/rtl8831 likewise maps b831 to RTL8851B.
This enables a conditional real-hardware trial, not an ABI or AP success claim.
B832 is RTL8852BU and is deliberately excluded. No binary alias rewriting.

References:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/master/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/rtw8851bu.c
https://github.com/biglinux/rtl8831/blob/main/os_dep/linux/usb_intf.c
https://iptime.com/products/807?pd=1

--- a/os_dep/linux/usb_intf.c
+++ b/os_dep/linux/usb_intf.c
@@ -173,6 +173,10 @@
 #ifdef CONFIG_RTL8851B
 	/*=== Realtek demoboard ===*/
 	{USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDER_ID_REALTEK, 0xB851, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff), .driver_info = RTL8851B},
+	/* RTL8831BU shares RTL8851B implementation; never match RTL8852BU B832. */
+	{USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDER_ID_REALTEK, 0xB831, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff), .driver_info = RTL8851B},
+	{USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(0x2001, 0x332A, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff), .driver_info = RTL8851B},
+	{USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(0x2C4E, 0x0128, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff), .driver_info = RTL8851B},
 
 	/*=== TP Link TX10UB AX900 ===*/
 	{USB_DEVICE_AND_INTERFACE_INFO(USB_VENDOR_ID_TPLINK, 0x010B, 0xff, 0xff, 0xff), .driver_info = RTL8851B},
